# Mirrors netlify.toml's [[redirects]] rules.
#
# netlify.toml lives one directory ABOVE frontend/, so it is invisible to a
# manual "drag the frontend folder into Netlify" deploy — Netlify only reads
# config from inside the folder you actually upload. This file is the
# equivalent config in the plain-text format Netlify also supports, placed
# directly in the published folder, so clean URLs (/event, /sell, etc.) work
# under either deploy method.
#
# If these two ever drift, netlify.toml is source of truth — regenerate this
# file from it rather than hand-editing both.

